(gen_random_uuid(), 'jk-bank-po-banking-associate-1397-posts-20261113', 'asia', 'India',
'J&K Bank PO and Banking Associate Recruitment 2026: 1,397 Posts, Apply by 26 November',
'जे एन्ड के बैंक पीओ र बैंकिङ एसोसिएट भर्ना २०२६: १,३९७ पद, आवेदन २६ नोभेम्बरसम्म',
'J&K Bank PO and Banking Associate Recruitment 2026: 1,397 posts for J&K and Ladakh domicile graduates. Apply online at jkb.bank.in by 26 November 2026.',
'जे एन्ड के बैंक पीओ र बैंकिङ एसोसिएट भर्ना २०२६ मा जम्मू कश्मीर र लद्दाखका स्नातकका लागि १,३९७ पद खुलेका छन्। आवेदन jkb.bank.in बाट २६ नोभेम्बर २०२६ सम्म अनलाइन मात्र दिन सकिन्छ।',
$$<p>J&K Bank PO and Banking Associate Recruitment 2026 has opened 1,397 posts for graduates who hold domicile of Jammu and Kashmir or Ladakh, and the application window is open now, from 7 November to 26 November 2026. Of the 1,397 posts, 343 are for Probationary Officers and 1,054 are for Banking Associates, split between the two Union Territories. You apply online only, through the Careers section of jkb.bank.in, and the fee must also be paid by 26 November 2026. The Institute of Banking Personnel Selection conducts the online examinations, so the selection follows the familiar IBPS pattern: a single online test for Banking Associates, and prelims, mains and an interview for Probationary Officers. For a graduate living in Jammu and Kashmir or Ladakh, this is the largest bank recruitment in the region this year.</p>
<table><tr><th>At a glance</th><th>J&K Bank PO and Banking Associate 2026</th></tr><tr><td>Organisation</td><td>Jammu and Kashmir Bank Ltd</td></tr><tr><td>Posts</td><td>1,397 — Probationary Officer 343, Banking Associate 1,054</td></tr><tr><td>Advertisements</td><td>JKB/HR/Rectt/2026-492 to JKB/HR/Rectt/2026-495</td></tr><tr><td>Notification</td><td>6 November 2026</td></tr><tr><td>Application dates</td><td>7 to 26 November 2026</td></tr><tr><td>Application route</td><td>Online only at jkb.bank.in, Careers section</td></tr><tr><td>Application fee</td><td>PO Rs 1,000 / Rs 1,200; BA Rs 600 / Rs 800, plus GST, non-refundable</td></tr><tr><td>Age limit</td><td>20 to 30 years as on 1 January 2026</td></tr><tr><td>Qualification</td><td>Graduate in any discipline</td></tr><tr><td>Domicile</td><td>Jammu and Kashmir or Ladakh only, against that Union Territory advertisement</td></tr><tr><td>Selection</td><td>IBPS online examinations, document verification, and interview for Probationary Officer</td></tr><tr><td>Examination dates</td><td>Not announced</td></tr><tr><td>Pay</td><td>Probationary Officer starting basic Rs 48,480; Banking Associate starting basic Rs 24,050</td></tr></table>
<h2>J&K Bank PO and Banking Associate Recruitment 2026: the two posts in detail</h2>
<h2>What it offers — Probationary Officer and Banking Associate</h2>
<p>The Probationary Officer post is the officer entry into the bank, in Junior Management Grade Scale I. The starting basic pay is Rs 48,480 a month, in the scale of Rs 48,480 to Rs 85,920, with the allowances that apply to officers on top of the basic pay. Probation lasts two years, and a service bond of Rs 2 lakh applies. Probationary Officers are trained for branch and administrative work and move into officer roles on confirmation, so the post suits graduates who want a banking career rather than a short-term job. Of the 343 Probationary Officer posts, 323 are for Jammu and Kashmir and 20 are for Ladakh, under separate advertisements for the two Union Territories.</p>
<p>The Banking Associate post is the front-line role of the bank, the staff customers meet first at the branch. The starting basic pay is Rs 24,050 a month, in the scale of Rs 24,050 to Rs 64,480, with allowances on top. Probation lasts six months, and a service bond of Rs 1 lakh applies. The work is customer facing — accounts, cash, deposits and the day-to-day work of a branch — and the post suits a graduate who wants a steady bank job without the longer officer probation. Of the 1,054 Banking Associate posts, 1,033 are for Jammu and Kashmir and 21 are for Ladakh.</p>
<p>The 1,397 posts come through four separate advertisements, numbered JKB/HR/Rectt/2026-492 to JKB/HR/Rectt/2026-495, under a notification dated 6 November 2026. Two advertisements cover the Probationary Officer posts and two cover the Banking Associate posts, one for each Union Territory in each case. Apply only against the advertisement of your own Union Territory.</p>
<h2>Who can apply — age, degree and domicile</h2>
<p>The age limit is 20 to 30 years as on 1 January 2026. The qualification is a graduation degree in any discipline, so the stream of your degree does not matter — arts, science, commerce and professional degrees all qualify, provided you hold a degree from a recognised institution.</p>
<p>The condition that decides most applications is domicile. Only candidates who hold domicile of Jammu and Kashmir or Ladakh can apply, and you must apply against the advertisement of your own Union Territory. A candidate from Jammu and Kashmir cannot apply for a Ladakh post, and a candidate from Ladakh cannot apply for a Jammu and Kashmir post. Candidates from other states and Union Territories cannot apply for either. If your domicile certificate is not ready, get it in order before 26 November, because the application form will ask for it and the bank will check it at document verification.</p>
<h2>How to apply</h2>
<p>Apply only at jkb.bank.in, through the Careers section, between 7 November and 26 November 2026. Choose the advertisement for your Union Territory and your post, register with your details, fill in the form carefully, and upload the documents the form asks for. Pay the fee online before you submit the form, and keep a copy of your confirmation page and registration number. The fee must be paid by 26 November 2026 as well — a form without the fee is not a complete application.</p>
<p>The fee carries Goods and Services Tax on top, and it is non-refundable. For Probationary Officer, the fee is Rs 1,000 for Scheduled Caste, Scheduled Tribe, SEBC and Persons with Benchmark Disabilities candidates, and Rs 1,200 for all other candidates. For Banking Associate, the fee is Rs 600 for Scheduled Caste, Scheduled Tribe, SEBC, Persons with Benchmark Disabilities and Ex-Servicemen candidates, and Rs 800 for all other candidates. One warning on the fee, because the web disagrees on it: one source, CareerIndia, lists the Probationary Officer concessional fee as Rs 1,200, but Testbook, ET BFSI, GovtJobsAlert and other sources agree that it is Rs 1,000. This article uses Rs 1,000, and you should confirm the fee from the detailed notification on the bank website before you pay.</p>
<p>Do not leave the form to the last day. The window closes on 26 November 2026, and bank portals slow down badly in the last two days as thousands of candidates apply at once. A form left half filled at the deadline will not be accepted.</p>
<h2>What the notification does not say</h2>
<p>Three things are worth knowing before you apply. First, the examination dates have not been announced. The bank has said only that the Institute of Banking Personnel Selection will conduct the online examinations — no dates for the Banking Associate test, the Probationary Officer prelims or the mains have been given, so do not trust any date you see on an unofficial page. Second, the category-wise vacancy split for each of the four advertisements was not fully read for this article, so this article does not give a post-by-post reservation table. The detailed notification carries the split, and you should read it to see the numbers for your own category. Third, the selection pattern given here is the summary pattern — the Banking Associate test is a single 100-mark online exam of 60 minutes, covering English, quantitative aptitude and reasoning, followed by document verification, while the Probationary Officer route is prelims at 100 marks, which is qualifying, then mains at 200 objective marks plus 25 descriptive marks, then an interview.</p>
<p>One more condition to note: the bond amounts are Rs 2 lakh for Probationary Officers and Rs 1 lakh for Banking Associates, and the probation periods are two years and six months. The exact refund or release condition of the bond is not spelled out in the sources read, so check the notification and the appointment letter for the terms.</p>
<p>Never pay anyone to apply for these posts. The only genuine fee is the one named in the notification — Rs 1,000 or Rs 1,200 for Probationary Officer and Rs 600 or Rs 800 for Banking Associate, plus Goods and Services Tax — payable online only through the official bank portal. No agent, no coaching centre and no person on social media can offer you a post in this recruitment, and anyone who asks for money for a seat or a guaranteed selection is trying to cheat you.</p>
<p>If you are tracking other large recruitments, the <a href="https://growentix.cloud/articles/rrb-ntpc-undergraduate-1688-posts-20261109">RRB NTPC Undergraduate Recruitment 2026 has 1,688 posts, with applications closing on 13 November</a>, and the <a href="https://growentix.cloud/articles/mpsc-group-c-services-16717-posts-20261111">MPSC Group C Services recruitment has 16,717 posts, with applications opening on 13 November</a>. Both follow the same pattern of a short window and a large number of posts, so the same advice applies: apply early and read the notification first.</p>
<p>Sources: Testbook, "J&K Bank PO and Banking Associate Recruitment 2026", 2026; ET BFSI, "J&K Bank Recruitment 2026: Apply Online for 1,397 PO and Banking Associate Posts", 2026; GovtJobsAlert, "J&K Bank PO and Banking Associate Recruitment 2026", 2026; Viksit Haryana, "J&K Bank Recruitment 2026: 1,397 PO and Banking Associate Posts", 2026; CareerIndia, "J&K Bank Recruitment 2026: Apply Online for 1,397 PO and Associate Posts", 2026. NOTE: one source, CareerIndia, lists the Probationary Officer concessional fee as Rs 1,200; the other sources agree it is Rs 1,000, and this article uses Rs 1,000. Readers should confirm the fee, the vacancy split and the examination dates from the detailed notification on jkb.bank.in. Apply only through jkb.bank.in.</p>$$,
$$<p>जे एन्ड के बैंक पीओ र बैंकिङ एसोसिएट भर्ना २०२६ मा जम्मू कश्मीर वा लद्दाखको अधिवास भएका स्नातकका लागि १,३९७ पद खुलेका छन्, र आवेदन ७ नोभेम्बरदेखि २६ नोभेम्बर २०२६ सम्म खुला छ। यीमध्ये प्रोबेशनरी अफिसर ३४३ र बैंकिङ एसोसिएट १,०५४ पद छन्। आवेदन jkb.bank.in को करिअर खण्डबाट अनलाइन मात्र दिन सकिन्छ, र शुल्क पनि २६ नोभेम्बरसम्म तिर्नुपर्छ। अनलाइन परीक्षा इन्स्टिच्युट अफ बैंकिङ पर्सोनेल सिलेक्सनले लिन्छ — बैंकिङ एसोसिएटका लागि एउटा अनलाइन परीक्षा, प्रोबेशनरी अफिसरका लागि प्रिलिम्स, मेन्स र अन्तर्वार्ता। जम्मू कश्मीर वा लद्दाखमा बस्ने स्नातकका लागि यो वर्षको सबैभन्दा ठूलो बैंक भर्ना हो,</p>
