(gen_random_uuid(), 'jshps-recruitment-637-posts-20261113', 'asia', 'India',
'JSHPS Recruitment 2026: 637 Posts, Apply by 4 December',
'JSHPS भर्ती 2026: 637 पद, 4 डिसेम्बरसम्म आवेदन दिनुहोस्',
'JSHPS has opened 637 contractual posts in Jharkhand horticulture. Online applications close 4 December 2026 at 3 pm, with a hard-copy deadline on 14 December.',
'झारखण्ड हर्टिकल्चर प्रवर्द्धन सोसाइटीले 637 करार पदका लागि आवेदन मागेको छ। अनलाइन आवेदन 4 डिसेम्बर 2026 दिउँसो 3 बजेसम्म खुला छ र छापिएको आवेदन 14 डिसेम्बरसम्म पुग्नुपर्छ।',
$$<p><strong>JSHPS Recruitment 2026</strong> has opened 637 contractual posts in the Jharkhand State Horticulture Promotion Society, under the Directorate of Horticulture in the Government of Jharkhand. The recruitment covers a wide spread of jobs, from block level programme management and data entry work to district level management and senior posts, and the application window is already open. Online applications close at 3 pm on 4 December 2026, and that is not the end of the process. Every applicant must also send a printed copy of the application, with the prescribed documents, so that it reaches the designated office by 5 pm on 14 December 2026. An online submission on its own does not complete the application, and this is the single most important detail in this recruitment. Readers who treat 14 December as the online last date, or who treat 4 December as the only deadline, will both be mistaken, and the difference matters. This article sets out the posts, the pay, the eligibility rules and the two deadlines, and it also states clearly what the notification does not say, so that applicants can check the official advertisement before they apply.</p> <h2>At a glance</h2> <table> <tr><th>Detail</th><th>What we know</th></tr> <tr><td>Organisation</td><td>Jharkhand State Horticulture Promotion Society, Directorate of Horticulture, Government of Jharkhand</td></tr> <tr><td>Advertisement</td><td>Advt No. 01/2026</td></tr> <tr><td>Total posts</td><td>637 contractual posts</td></tr> <tr><td>Apply online</td><td>4 November to 4 December 2026, until 3 pm, at recruitment.jharkhand.gov.in</td></tr> <tr><td>Hard-copy deadline</td><td>Printed application with prescribed documents must reach the designated office by 5 pm on 14 December 2026</td></tr> <tr><td>Application fee</td><td>Not stated in the sources read</td></tr> <tr><td>Selection process</td><td>Not stated in the sources read</td></tr> <tr><td>Pay</td><td>Consolidated Rs 20,000 to Rs 1,00,000 a month, by post, with a 5 per cent performance-linked annual increment</td></tr> </table> <h2>JSHPS Recruitment 2026: What it offers</h2> <p>The 637 posts are spread across several groups, and the advertisement gives the numbers for the largest groups. Block Program Manager accounts for 264 posts, and Assistant-cum-Data Entry Operator accounts for 290 posts, made up of 264 posts at block level and 26 posts at headquarters and district level. District Program Manager accounts for 24 posts and District Accountant also accounts for 24 posts. Deputy Director accounts for 3 posts and the headquarters Accountant accounts for 2 posts. The remaining posts, around 30 in number, sit in the other groups named in the advertisement, including State Program Manager, MIS Officer and Thematic Expert, and the full post-wise split is set out in the notification itself. Taken together, the named groups total 607 posts, and the balance of 30 posts belongs to those other groups, so the total of 637 is reached when every group is counted.</p> <p>Pay is consolidated, which means a fixed monthly amount for the post, and it runs from Rs 20,000 a month at the lower end to Rs 1,00,000 a month at the top. Deputy Director is the highest paid post in the recruitment, on a consolidated Rs 1,00,000 a month. State Program Manager and MIS Officer are on a consolidated Rs 60,000 a month. The other posts fall between those figures according to the post-wise pay given in the advertisement, and the notification also provides for a 5 per cent performance-linked annual increment. That increment is tied to performance, so it is not an automatic yearly rise on the same terms as a regular pay scale, and applicants should not read the consolidated figure as the same thing as a regular government salary with dearness allowance and the other usual allowances.</p> <p>For readers who are watching other government recruitment, the pattern here is familiar: a large number of posts at the field level, a smaller number of supervisory and specialist posts, and a single online portal for applications. Readers following health recruitment in the same state may also want to read the <a href='https://growentix.cloud/articles/nepal-telecom-recruitment-80-posts-20261112'>Nepal Telecom recruitment for 80 permanent posts</a> and the <a href='https://growentix.cloud/articles/dsssb-je-mts-1260-posts-20261112'>DSSSB JE and MTS recruitment for 1,260 posts</a>, which were published on Growentix with the same style of post-wise detail and the same warning about checking the official notification before applying.</p> <h2>Who can apply</h2> <p>Eligibility is post-wise, and the age limits, the qualifications and the experience required all change with the post. For Block Program Manager, the age limit is 21 to 30 years, and the qualification is a B.Sc. in Agriculture or Horticulture from an ICAR-recognised institution, with a postgraduate qualification described as desirable.</p> <p>For District Program Manager, State Program Manager, Thematic Expert and Accountant, the age limit is 30 to 45 years. For the Accountant post, the qualification is B.Com or M.Com in first class, together with Tally and three years of experience. For Deputy Director, the age limit is 35 to 50 years, and the qualification is a postgraduate degree in Agriculture or Horticulture, or an MBA in Agri-Business, together with ten years of experience, of which seven years must be in a supervisory role. The age relaxations given in the sources are an addition of 3 years for BC-I and BC-II candidates, an addition of 5 years for SC and ST candidates, and an addition of 3 years for women candidates.</p> <p>There is one point on age that applicants must be careful about, because the sources read for this article do not agree on it. One source says that age is counted as on 1 August 2026, and another source says that age is counted as on 4 December 2026. This article does not choose one of those dates over the other, because the disagreement is real and it is the official advertisement that settles it. An applicant whose age is close to the upper limit for the post they want could be eligible on one date and ineligible on the other, so this is not a small detail. Before applying, every applicant should open the official advertisement and check the exact date on which age is counted, and should work out eligibility on that date alone.</p> <h2>How to apply</h2> <p>Applications are made online at recruitment.jharkhand.gov.in. The online window runs from 4 November 2026 to 4 December 2026, and it closes at 3 pm on the last date. Applicants should complete the online form well before that time, because the portal is likely to be busy in the final hours, and a form that is still incomplete at 3 pm on 4 December will not count.</p> <p>The second stage is the part that applicants most often miss. An online submission alone does not complete the application. The printed application, together with the prescribed documents, must reach the designated office by 5 pm on 14 December 2026. That is a hard deadline for the physical papers, not an extension of the online window, and an application whose papers arrive after that time will not be complete. This is also the reason why one aggregator lists 14 December as the last date: that date is the hard-copy date, and the online form itself closes on 4 December. Applicants should therefore work to two deadlines, not one.</p> <h2>What the notification does not say</h2> <p>There are three important things that the sources read for this article do not state, and this article will not fill those gaps by guessing. First, the application fee is not stated in the sources read. No fee figure is given, and no statement is made about a fee exemption for any category, so this article gives no fee at all. Second, the selection process is not stated in the sources read. Third, the age cut-off date is in conflict between the sources, as set out above, with 1 August 2026 in one source and 4 December 2026 in another.</p> <p>Other details are also left to the advertisement. The category-wise split of the vacancies is given in the notification tables, but it was not fully reproduced in the sources read, so this article does not give a category-wise table. The exact place of posting for each post, the period of the contract and the conditions for its continuation are matters for the advertisement as well. None of that changes the two deadlines or the post-wise eligibility set out above, but it does mean that applicants should treat this article as a guide to the advertisement, not as a replacement for it.</p> <p>Do not pay anyone to apply for this recruitment. The application is made on the official portal at recruitment.jharkhand.gov.in, and no agent, no middleman and no social media account can improve the chances of an application or arrange a post.</p> <p>Sources: <a href='https://govtjobsalert.in/jshps-recruitment-2026/'>govtjobsalert.in</a>, <a href='https://freejobalert.com/articles/jshps-recruitment-2026-apply-online-for-637-assistant-deo-and-more-posts-3077868'>freejobalert.com</a>, <a href='https://govtjobalerts.org/news/jshps-recruitment-2026'>govtjobalerts.org</a>, <a href='https://preptm.com/jobs/jshps-recruitment-2026'>preptm.com</a></p>$$,
$$<p><strong>JSHPS Recruitment 2026</strong> अन्तर्गत झारखण्ड राज्य हर्टिकल्चर प्रवर्द्धन सोसाइटीमा 637 करार पदका लागि आवेदन मागिएको छ। यो सोसाइटी झारखण्ड सरकारको हर्टिकल्चर निर्देशनालय अन्तर्गत काम गर्छ। भर्तीमा ब्लक तहको कार्यक्रम व्यवस्थापन र डाटा इन्ट्रीदेखि जिल्ला तहको व्यवस्थापन र वरिष्ठ पदसम्म समेटिएका छन्, र आवेदनको समयावधि खुलिसकेको छ। अनलाइन आवेदन 4 डिसेम्बर 2026 दिउँसो 3 बजेसम्म खुला छ, र त्यहीँ प्रक्रिया सकिँदैन। हरेक आवेदकले छापिएको आवेदन तोकिएका कागजातसहित तोकिएको कार्यालयमा 14 डिसेम्बर 2026 साँझ 5 बजेसम्म पुग्ने गरी पठाउनुपर्छ। अनलाइन आवेदन मात्रले आवेदन पूरा हुँदैन, र यो नै यस भर्तीको सबैभन्दा महत्त्वपूर्ण कुरा हो।</p> <h2>एक नजरमा</h2> <table> <tr><th>विवरण</th><th>जानकारी</th></tr> <tr><td>संस्था</td><td>झारखण्ड राज्य हर्टिकल्चर प्रवर्द्धन सोसाइटी, हर्टिकल्चर निर्देशनालय, झारखण्ड सरकार</td></tr> <tr><td>विज्ञापन</td><td>Advt No. 01/2026</td></tr> <tr><td>कुल पद</td><td>637 करार पद</td></tr> <tr><td>अनलाइन आवेदन</td><td>4 नोभेम्बरदेखि 4 डिसेम्बर 2026, दिउँसो 3 बजेसम्म, recruitment.jharkhand.gov.in मा</td></tr> <tr><td>छापिएको आवेदनको मिति</td><td>छापिएको आवेदन तोकिएका कागजातसहित तोकिएको कार्यालयमा 14 डिसेम्बर 2026 साँझ 5 बजेसम्म पुग्नुपर्छ</td></tr> <tr><td>आवेदन शुल्क</td><td>पढिएका स्रोतहरूमा उल्लेख छैन</td></tr> <tr><td>छनोट प्रक्रिया</td><td>पढिएका स्रोतहरूमा उल्लेख छैन</td></tr> <tr><td>तलब</td><td>पदअनुसार समेकित मासिक रु. 20,000 देखि रु. 1,00,000 सम्म, कार्यसम्पादनमा आधारित वार्षिक 5 प्रतिशत वृद्धि</td></tr> </table> <h2>JSHPS Recruitment 2026: के प्रस्ताव छ</h2> <p>637 पदहरू विभिन्न समूहमा फैलिएका छन्, र विज्ञापनमा ठूला समूहहरूको संख्या दिइएको छ। ब्लक प्रोग्राम म्यानेजरमा 264 पद छन्, र असिस्टेन्ट-कम-डाटा इन्ट्री अपरेटरमा 290 पद छन्, जसमा ब्लक तहमा 264 र मुख्यालय तथा जिल्ला तहमा 26 पद छन्। डिस्ट्रिक्ट प्रोग्राम म्यानेजरमा 24 पद र डिस्ट्रिक्ट अकाउन्टेन्टमा पनि 24 पद छन्। डेपुटी डाइरेक्टरमा 3 पद र मुख्यालयको अकाउन्टेन्टमा 2 पद छन्। बाँकी पदहरू, करिब 30 वटा, विज्ञापनमा नाम दिइएका अन्य समूहहरूमा छन्, जसमा स्टेट प्रोग्राम म्यानेजर, एमआईएस अफिसर र थिम्याटिक एक्सपर्ट पनि पर्छन्, र पूर्ण पदअनुसार विवरण विज्ञापनमै दिइएको छ।</p> <p>तलब समेकित हुन्छ, अर्थात् पदका लागि तोकिएको निश्चित मासिक रकम हो, र यो मासिक रु. 20,000 देखि रु. 1,00,000 सम्म छ। यस भर्तीमा सबैभन्दा बढी तलब पाउने पद डेपुटी डाइरेक्टर हो, समेकित मासिक रु. 1,00,000। स्टेट प्रोग्राम म्यानेजर र एमआईएस अफिसरको समेकित तलब मासिक रु. 60,000 छ। अन्य पदहरूको तलब विज्ञापनमा दिइएको पदअनुसारको तलबअनुसार यी दुई आँकडाबीच पर्छ, र विज्ञापनमा कार्यसम्पादनमा आधारित वार्षिक 5 प्रतिशत वृद्धिको व्यवस्था पनि छ। यो वृद्धि कार्यसम्पादनसँग जोडिएको छ, त्यसैले यो नियमित तलबमानमा हुने स्वचालित वार्षिक वृद्धिजस्तो होइन, र आवेदकले समेकित आँकडालाई महँगी भत्ता र अन्य सामान्य भत्तासहितको नियमित सरकारी तलब ठान्नुहुँदैन।</p> <p>झारखण्डकै भर्ती पोर्टल recruitment.jharkhand.gov.in बाट आवेदन दिइन्छ, जुन पोर्टल राज्यका अन्य भर्तीहरूमा पनि प्रयोग हुन्छ, त्यसैले हालै अर्को झारखण्ड पदका लागि आवेदन दिएका आवेदकलाई प्रक्रिया परिचित लाग्नेछ। अन्य सरकारी भर्ती हेर्दै गर्ने पाठकहरूले ग्रोवेन्टिक्समा प्रकाशित <a href='https://growentix.cloud/articles/nepal-telecom-recruitment-80-posts-20261112'>नेपाल टेलिकमको 80 स्थायी पदको भर्ती</a> र <a href='https://growentix.cloud/articles/dsssb-je-mts-1260-posts-20261112'>डीएसएसएसबी जेई र एमटीएसको 1,260 पदको भर्ती</a> पनि हेर्न सक्छन्, जसमा त्यही शैलीमा पदअनुसार विवरण र आधिकारिक विज्ञापन हेर्ने चेतावनी दिइएको छ।</p> <h2>कसले आवेदन दिन सक्छ</h2> <p>योग्यता पदअनुसार फरक हुन्छ, र उमेर सीमा, योग्यता र अनुभव सबै पदसँगै बदलिन्छन्। ब्लक प्रोग्राम म्यानेजरका लागि उमेर सीमा 21 देखि 30 वर्ष छ, र योग्यता आईसीएआर मान्यता प्राप्त संस्थाबाट कृषि वा हर्टिकल्चरमा बीएस्सी हो, स्नातकोत्तर योग्यता भए राम्रो मानिन्छ। असिस्टेन्ट-कम-डाटा इन्ट्री अपरेटरका लागि उमेर सीमा 25 देखि 35 वर्ष छ, र योग्यता एडीसीए सहितको स्नातक, वा बीसीए, वा आईटीमा बीएस्सी हो, साथै ब्लक तहमा एक वर्ष र मुख्यालय तथा जिल्ला तहमा दुई वर्षको अनुभव चाहिन्छ।</p> <p>डिस्ट्रिक्ट प्रोग्राम म्यानेजर, स्टेट प्रोग्राम म्यानेजर, थिम्याटिक एक्सपर्ट र अकाउन्टेन्टका लागि उमेर सीमा 30 देखि 45 वर्ष छ। अकाउन्टेन्ट पदका लागि योग्यता प्रथम श्रेणीमा बीकम वा एमकम हो, साथै ट्याली र तीन वर्षको अनुभव चाहिन्छ। डेपुटी डाइरेक्टरका लागि उमेर सीमा 35 देखि 50 वर्ष छ, र योग्यता कृषि वा हर्टिकल्चरमा स्नातकोत्तर, वा कृषि व्यवसायमा एमबीए हो, साथै दश वर्षको अनुभव चाहिन्छ, जसमध्ये सात वर्ष निरीक्षणको भूमिकामा हुनुपर्छ। स्रोतहरूमा दिइएको उमेर छुटअनुसार बीसी-वन र बीसी-टू उम्मेदवारलाई 3 वर्ष, एससी र एसटी उम्मेदवारलाई 5 वर्ष, र महिला उम्मेदवारलाई 3 वर्ष छुट मिल्छ।</p> <p>उमेरबारे एउटा कुरामा आवेदकले सावधानी अपनाउनुपर्छ, किनकि यस लेखका लागि पढिएका स्रोतहरू यसमा सहमत छैनन्। एउटा स्रोतले उमेर 1 अगस्ट 2026 का आधारमा गनिने बताएको छ, र अर्को स्रोतले उमेर 4 डिसेम्बर 2026 का आधारमा गनिने बताएको छ। यस लेखले यी दुई मितिमध्ये एउटालाई अर्कोभन्दा सही ठानेको छैन, किनकि असहमति वास्तविक छ र यसको निर्णय आधिकारिक विज्ञापनले मात्र गर्छ। आफूले चाहेको पदको माथिल्लो उमेर सीमाको नजिक रहेको आवेदक एउटा मितिमा योग्य र अर्को मितिमा अयोग्य हुन सक्छ, त्यसैले यो सानो कुरा होइन। आवेदन दिनुअघि हरेक आवेदकले आधिकारिक विज्ञापन खोलेर उमेर कुन मितिका आधारमा गनिन्छ भनेर हेर्नुपर्छ, र योग्यता त्यही मितिका आधारमा मात्र हिसाब गर्नुपर्छ।</p> <h2>कसरी आवेदन दिने</h2> <p>आवेदन अनलाइन recruitment.jharkhand.gov.in मा दिइन्छ। अनलाइन समयावधि 4 नोभेम्बर 2026 देखि 4 डिसेम्बर 2026 सम्म छ, र अन्तिम दिन दिउँसो 3 बजे बन्द हुन्छ। आवेदकले त्यो समयभन्दा धेरै अगाडि नै अनलाइन फारम भर्नुपर्छ, किनकि अन्तिम घण्टाहरूमा पोर्टलमा भीड हुने सम्भावना छ, र 4 डिसेम्बर दिउँसो 3 बजेसम्म अधुरो रहेको फारम गणना हुँदैन।</p> <p>दोस्रो चरण नै आवेदकहरूले प्रायः छुटाउने भाग हो। अनलाइन आवेदन मात्रले आवेदन पूरा हुँदैन। छापिएको आवेदन, तोकिएका कागजातसहित, तोकिएको कार्यालयमा 14 डिसेम्बर 2026 साँझ 5 बजेसम्म पुग्नुपर्छ। पहिले, 4 डिसेम्बर दिउँसो 3 बजेअघि अनलाइन फारम बुझाउनुहोस्। दोस्रो, छापिएको आवेदन कागजातसहित 14 डिसेम्बर साँझ 5 बजेअघि पुग्ने गरी पठाउनुहोस्।</p> <h2>विज्ञापनमा के भनिएको छैन</h2> <p>यस लेखका लागि पढिएका स्रोतहरूमा नभनिएका तीनवटा महत्त्वपूर्ण कुरा छन्, र यो लेखले अनुमान गरेर ती खाली ठाउँ भर्ने छैन। पहिलो, आवेदन शुल्क पढिएका स्रोतहरूमा भनिएको छैन। दोस्रो, छनोट प्रक्रिया पढिएका स्रोतहरूमा भनिएको छैन। तेस्रो, उमेर गणना गर्ने मिति स्रोतहरूबीच द्वन्द्वमा छ, जसको बारेमा माथि लेखिएको छ, एउटा स्रोतमा 1 अगस्ट 2026 र अर्कोमा 4 डिसेम्बर 2026 छ।</p> <p>अन्य विवरणहरू पनि विज्ञापनमा नै छोडिएका छन्। यस लेखका स्रोतहरू अन्त्यमा सूचीबद्ध छन्, र आवेदन दिनुअघि भर्ती पोर्टलबाट आधिकारिक विज्ञापन खोल्नुपर्छ।</p> <p>यस भर्तीका लागि आवेदन दिन कसैलाई पैसा नतिर्नुहोस्। आवेदन आधिकारिक पोर्टल recruitment.jharkhand.gov.in मा दिइन्छ, र कुनै एजेन्ट, बिचौलिया वा सामाजिक सञ्जाल खाताले आवेदनको सम्भावना बढाउन वा पद मिलाउन सक्दैन।</p> <p>स्रोतहरू: <a href='https://govtjobsalert.in/jshps-recruitment-2026/'>govtjobsalert.in</a>, <a href='https://freejobalert.com/articles/jshps-recruitment-2026-apply-online-for-637-assistant-deo-and-more-posts-3077868'>freejobalert.com</a>, <a href='https://govtjobalerts.org/news/jshps-recruitment-2026'>govtjobalerts.org</a>, <a href='https://preptm.com/jobs/jshps-recruitment-2026'>preptm.com</a></p>$$,
ARRAY['https://govtjobsalert.in/jshps-recruitment-2026/', 'https://freejobalert.com/articles/jshps-recruitment-2026-apply-online-for-637-assistant-deo-and-more-posts-3077868', 'https://govtjobalerts.org/news/jshps-recruitment-2026', 'https://preptm.com/jobs/jshps-recruitment-2026'], NOW(), NOW(), NOW()) ON CONFLICT ("slug") DO NOTHING;

-- chhattisgarh-state-power-recruitment-1501-posts-20261113 (English 1761 words; Nepali 874 words)
INSERT INTO "Article" ("id", "slug", "category", "country", "titleEn", "titleNe", "excerptEn", "excerptNe", "bodyEn", "bodyNe", "sources", "publishedAt", "createdAt", "updatedAt")
VALUES
(gen_random_uuid(), 'chhattisgarh-state-power-recruitment-1501-posts-20261113', 'asia', 'India',
'Chhattisgarh State Power Recruitment 2026: 1,501 Posts, Apply by 26 November',
'छत्तीसगढ स्टेट पावर भर्ती 2026: 1,501 पदहरू, 26 नोभेम्बरसम्म आवेदन दिनुहोस्',
'Chhattisgarh State Power has opened 1,501 posts across three power companies. Apply online at cspc.co.in by 26 November 2026; fees run from Rs 200 to Rs 800.',
'छत्तीसगढ स्टेट पावरले तीनवटा विद्युत कम्पनीमा 1,501 पदहरू खोलेको छ। 26 नोभेम्बर 2026 सम्म cspc.co.in बाट अनलाइन आवेदन दिनुहोस्।',
$$<p>Chhattisgarh State Power Recruitment 2026 has opened 1,501 posts across the three state power companies, and online applications are already open. The Chhattisgarh State Power Transmission Company Ltd (CSPTCL), Raipur, is running the recruitment for the Chhattisgarh State Power Distribution Company Ltd (CSPDCL), CSPTCL and the Chhattisgarh State Power Generation Company Ltd (CSPGCL) together, under two advertisements issued on 5 November 2026. Candidates can apply online only at cspc.co.in until 11:55 pm on 26 November 2026. With 609 Data Entry Operator posts, 300 Attendant posts, 216 Junior Engineer posts and 152 Assistant Engineer posts, this is one of the largest state power recruitments of the year, so check eligibility first.</p><p>The recruitment is split into two advertisements: No. 1/2026 for Class-II posts and No. 2/2026 for Class-III and Class-IV posts, offering 195 and 1,306 posts respectively. The window opened at 8:00 pm on 6 November 2026 and closes at 11:55 pm on 26 November 2026, and the fee must also be paid by that deadline. There is no offline form; the whole process runs through the Recruitment section of cspc.co.in.</p><h2>Chhattisgarh State Power Recruitment 2026: At a glance</h2><table><tr><th>Organisation</th><td>Chhattisgarh State Power Transmission Company Ltd (CSPTCL), Raipur, for CSPDCL, CSPTCL and CSPGCL</td></tr><tr><th>Advertisement</th><td>No. 1/2026 (Class-II) and No. 2/2026 (Class-III and IV), dated 5 November 2026</td></tr><tr><th>Total posts</th><td>1,501 (Class II 195, Class III and IV 1,306)</td></tr><tr><th>Apply dates</th><td>6 November 2026, 8:00 pm to 26 November 2026, 11:55 pm</td></tr><tr><th>Apply site</th><td>cspc.co.in (Recruitment section)</td></tr><tr><th>Fee</th><td>Rs 200 to Rs 800, by post group and category, online only, non-refundable</td></tr><tr><th>Age as on</th><td>1 January 2026</td></tr><tr><th>Selection</th><td>Online CBT, then interview, physical test, shorthand or typing test, and document verification as per the post</td></tr><tr><th>Pay</th><td>Basic pay Rs 14,800 to Rs 56,100, by post</td></tr></table><h2>What it offers</h2><p>The largest group is Data Entry Operator, with 609 posts across the three companies: 450 in CSPDCL, 95 in CSPGCL and 64 in CSPTCL. Next comes Attendant (Plant) Grade III with 300 posts, followed by Junior Engineer with 216 posts and Assistant Engineer with 152 posts. The remaining 224 posts cover officers, programmers, accounts officers, medical officers, stenographers, fire officers, law officers and other technical posts. Candidates should check the post-wise tables in the notification, because the duties, the company and the place of posting change from post to post.</p><p>Pay is fixed on the post-wise pay matrix, and the range is wide because the recruitment covers everything from Class-IV posts to Class-II officers. Basic pay starts at Rs 14,800 a month for Fire Attendant (S-1) and Rs 15,600 for Attendant (Plant) (S-2). A Data Entry Operator starts at Rs 19,800 (S-4). A Junior Engineer starts at Rs 35,400 (S-8). Assistant Engineers and specified Class-II officers in the O-1 scale start at Rs 56,100. These are regular posts in the state power companies, not a training scheme and not a fixed-term contract.</p><p>There is one condition that every selected candidate must accept. A four-year service bond applies, with a deposit to be paid at joining. The deposit is Rs 3,00,000 for Assistant Engineer, Rs 2,00,000 for Junior Engineer, Rs 1,00,000 for other Class-III posts and Rs 50,000 for Class-IV posts. The deposit is refundable after the agreement period, as stated in the notification. Candidates unwilling to serve the bond period should think carefully before applying.</p><p>Selection starts with an online computer based test (CBT) of 100 multiple choice questions for 100 marks, to be answered in two hours. Eighty questions come from the professional subject of the post and twenty cover general knowledge, English, Hindi, reasoning and quantitative aptitude. There is negative marking of 0.25 marks for every wrong answer, and the qualifying marks are 40 per cent for unreserved and OBC candidates and 30 per cent for SC and ST candidates. After the CBT, the process changes by post: some posts have an interview, a physical examination, shorthand test or typing skill test, and all end with document verification. Some posts also have an interview; Junior Engineers, law officers, medical support staff and Attendant posts are selected through the CBT and document verification only.</p><h2>Who can apply</h2><p>Age is counted as on 1 January 2026. The minimum age is 18 years for some posts and 21 years for others, depending on the post applied for. The maximum age for Assistant Engineer, Junior Engineer, Data Entry Operator and most other posts is 40 years for Chhattisgarh unreserved male candidates and 45 years for eligible Chhattisgarh female, SC, ST and OBC candidates. The limits are lower for the fire posts. Fire Officers and Sub Fire Officers have a maximum age of 30 years, rising to 35 years for the eligible categories, and Fire Attendants have a maximum of 25 years, rising to 30 years. Candidates must check the limit for their own post and category in the notification.</p><p>The domicile rule is the most important part of the eligibility conditions, and it catches many candidates out. Class-III and Class-IV posts are open only to candidates who hold Chhattisgarh domicile. For the eligible Class-II posts, candidates from outside Chhattisgarh may apply, but their upper age limit is 30 years. Anyone without Chhattisgarh domicile who wants a Class-III or Class-IV post such as Data Entry Operator or Attendant should not apply or pay the fee.</p><p>Qualifications are fixed post by post. An Assistant Engineer needs a four-year engineering degree or AMIE in the relevant discipline. A Junior Engineer needs a three-year engineering diploma. A Programmer needs engineering in computer science or information technology, or an MCA. An Accounts Officer needs to be a Chartered Accountant or a Cost Accountant. A Medical Officer needs an MBBS degree with registration. A Data Entry Operator needs a computer science or information technology qualification, or graduation with an accepted computer qualification. Attendant (Plant) needs a pass in Class 10 with at least a second division and a two-year ITI certificate in the trade. Several posts also ask for post-specific experience, registration, typing speed or shorthand. The qualification must be held on or before 26 November 2026.</p><p>Regular departmental employees of the three power companies are exempt from the fee. All other candidates pay online, and the fee is non-refundable. In the higher-fee group (Assistant Engineers, Junior Engineers, officers, programmers and similar posts) it is Rs 800 for unreserved candidates, Rs 700 for OBC and Rs 600 for SC and ST candidates. In the lower-fee group (Data Entry Operator, Stenographer, medical support posts, Attendant and similar posts) it is Rs 400 for unreserved, Rs 300 for OBC and Rs 200 for SC and ST candidates. Candidates must pay for the correct group, because a wrong payment will not be refunded.</p><h2>How to apply</h2><p>Applications are accepted online only, through the Recruitment section of cspc.co.in. Candidates should open the official site, find the recruitment link for Advertisement No. 1/2026 or No. 2/2026 as per the post, and register with a valid email address and mobile number. Personal, educational and domicile details must be filled in carefully, because corrections after submission are not promised. Scanned copies of the photograph, signature, certificates and domicile proof should be kept ready in the size and format the portal asks for.</p><p>After the form is filled in, the fee must be paid online before 11:55 pm on 26 November 2026. The portal accepts the usual online payment modes, and the payment receipt and the submitted application should both be saved and printed. Candidates should also note the reference number of the application, because it will be needed for the admit card and for any later communication. There is no need to send a printed copy by post, unless the notification for a particular post says otherwise.</p><p>Candidates looking for other live government openings on Growentix can also read <a href='https://growentix.cloud/articles/rrc-northern-railway-act-apprentice-4651-posts-20261112'>RRC Northern Railway Apprentice Recruitment 2026</a> and <a href='https://growentix.cloud/articles/mpsc-group-c-services-16717-posts-20261111'>MPSC Group C Services Recruitment 2026</a>, both of which are open for applications in November 2026.</p><h2>What the notification does not say</h2><p>The notification does not announce the date of the computer based test. It says only that the date will be announced later, so no date should be taken from any other website, and candidates should watch cspc.co.in for the admit card notice. The category-wise vacancy split, covering unreserved, SC, ST, OBC, female and ex-servicemen seats, is given in the tables of the official notification, but it was not fully reproduced in the sources read for this article. Readers should open the official PDF and check the table for their own post and category before applying. The post-wise tables in the notification, not any summary, are the final word.</p><p>Never pay anyone to apply for this recruitment. The only genuine fee is the online application fee paid on cspc.co.in, and no agent, coaching centre or social media account can arrange a post, a merit list place or an admit card. Anyone asking for money for selection, document verification or joining should be reported, and no document, password or payment should be shared with them.</p><p>Sources: https://www.freejobalert.com/articles/csptcl-recruitment-2026-apply-online-for-1501-ae-je-deo-attendant-and-more-posts-3079324, https://www.certifica.in/jobs/cg-power-ae-je-deo-attendant-recruitment-2026, https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/education/news/cg-state-power-company-recruitment-2026-apply-online-for-1501-ae-je-and-other-posts/articleshow/135629594.cms, https://www.9curry.com/notices/718d3f</p>$$,
$$<p>छत्तीसगढ स्टेट पावर भर्ती 2026 अन्तर्गत तीनवटा राज्य विद्युत कम्पनीमा 1,501 पदहरू खुलेका छन्, र अनलाइन आवेदन पहिले नै सुरु भइसकेको छ। छत्तीसगढ स्टेट पावर ट्रान्समिसन कम्पनी लिमिटेड (CSPTCL), रायपुरले छत्तीसगढ स्टेट पावर डिस्ट्रिब्युसन कम्पनी लिमिटेड (CSPDCL), CSPTCL र छत्तीसगढ स्टेट पावर जेनेरेसन कम्पनी लिमिटेड (CSPGCL) का लागि संयुक्त रूपमा यो भर्ती गरिरहेको छ। उम्मेदवारहरूले 26 नोभेम्बर 2026 राति 11:55 बजेसम्म cspc.co.in बाट मात्र अनलाइन आवेदन दिन सक्छन्। 609 डाटा इन्ट्री अपरेटर, 300 अटेन्डेन्ट, 216 जुनियर इन्जिनियर र 152 असिस्टेन्ट इन्जिनियर पद छन्।</p><p>भर्ती दुईवटा विज्ञापनमा बाँडिएको छ: विज्ञापन नम्बर 1/2026 क्लास-II का पदहरूका लागि र नम्बर 2/2026 क्लास-III र क्लास-IV का पदहरूका लागि हो, जसमा क्रमशः 195 र 1,306 पद छन्। आवेदन विन्डो 6 नोभेम्बर 2026 बेलुका 8:00 बजेबाट खुलेको हो र 26 नोभेम्बर 2026 राति 11:55 बजे बन्द हुन्छ। शुल्क पनि सोही मितिसम्म तिर्नुपर्छ। अफलाइन फाराम छैन; पूरै प्रक्रिया cspc.co.in को Recruitment खण्डबाट चल्छ।</p><h2>छत्तीसगढ स्टेट पावर भर्ती 2026: एक नजरमा</h2><table><tr><th>संस्था</th><td>छत्तीसगढ स्टेट पावर ट्रान्समिसन कम्पनी लिमिटेड (CSPTCL), रायपुर — CSPDCL, CSPTCL र CSPGCL का लागि</td></tr><tr><th>विज्ञापन</th><td>नम्बर 1/2026 (क्लास-II) र नम्बर 2/2026 (क्लास-III र IV), मिति 5 नोभेम्बर 2026</td></tr><tr><th>कूल पद</th><td>1,501 (क्लास-II 195, क्लास-III र IV 1,306)</td></tr><tr><th>आवेदन मिति</th><td>6 नोभेम्बर 2026 बेलुका 8:00 बजेदेखि 26 नोभेम्बर 2026 राति 11:55 बजेसम्म</td></tr><tr><th>आवेदन साइट</th><td>cspc.co.in (Recruitment खण्ड)</td></tr><tr><th>शुल्क</th><td>रु 200 देखि रु 800 सम्म, पद समूह र श्रेणी अनुसार, अनलाइन मात्र, फिर्ता हुँदैन</td></tr><tr><th>उमेर गणना</th><td>1 जनवरी 2026</td></tr><tr><th>छनोट</th><td>अनलाइन CBT, त्यसपछि अन्तर्वार्ता, शारीरिक परीक्षा, सर्टह्यान्ड वा टाइपिङ परीक्षा र कागजात जाँच</td></tr><tr><th>तलब</th><td>आधारभूत तलब रु 14,800 देखि रु 56,100 सम्म, पद अनुसार</td></tr></table><h2>के पाइन्छ</h2><p>सबैभन्दा ठूलो समूह डाटा इन्ट्री अपरेटर हो, जसमा तीनवटै कम्पनीमा गरी 609 पद छन्: CSPDCL मा 450, CSPGCL मा 95 र CSPTCL मा 64। त्यसपछि अटेन्डेन्ट (प्लान्ट) ग्रेड III का 300 पद, जुनियर इन्जिनियरका 216 पद र असिस्टेन्ट इन्जिनियरका 152 पद छन्। बाँकी 224 पदमा अधिकृत, प्रोग्रामर, लेखा र चिकित्सा अधिकृत, स्टेनोग्राफर र अन्य प्राविधिक पद छन्। पदअनुसारको तालिका सूचनामा हेर्नुहोस्।</p><p>तलब पदअनुसारको म्याट्रिक्समा तोकिएको छ। आधारभूत तलब फायर अटेन्डेन्ट (S-1) का लागि महिनाको रु 14,800 बाट सुरु हुन्छ र अटेन्डेन्ट (प्लान्ट) (S-2) का लागि रु 15,600 छ। डाटा इन्ट्री अपरेटरको सुरुको तलब रु 19,800 (S-4) छ। जुनियर इन्जिनियरको सुरुको तलब रु 35,400 (S-8) छ। असिस्टेन्ट इन्जिनियर र तोकिएका क्लास-II अधिकृतहरू (O-1) को सुरुको तलब रु 56,100 छ। यी राज्य विद्युत कम्पनीका नियमित पदहरू हुन्।</p><p>छनोट भएकालाई चार वर्षको सेवा बन्ड लागू हुन्छ, र धरौटी नियुक्तिको समयमा तिर्नुपर्छ। धरौटी असिस्टेन्ट इन्जिनियरका लागि रु 3,00,000, जुनियर इन्जिनियरका लागि रु 2,00,000, अन्य क्लास-III पदहरूका लागि रु 1,00,000 र क्लास-IV पदहरूका लागि रु 50,000 छ। धरौटी सम्झौता अवधि पूरा भएपछि फिर्ता हुन्छ। बन्ड अवधि पूरा गर्न नचाहनेले आवेदन दिनुअघि सोच्नुपर्छ।</p><p>छनोट CBT बाट सुरु हुन्छ: 100 बहुविकल्पीय प्रश्न, 100 अंक, दुई घण्टा। 80 प्रश्न पदको व्यावसायिक विषयबाट आउँछन्, र 20 प्रश्न सामान्य ज्ञान, अंग्रेजी, हिन्दी, तर्क र परिमाणात्मक योग्यताबाट आउँछन्। प्रत्येक गलत उत्तरमा 0.25 अंक कट्छ। उत्तीर्ण अंक अनारक्षित र OBC उम्मेदवारका लागि 40 प्रतिशत र SC र ST उम्मेदवारका लागि 30 प्रतिशत छ। CBT पछि पद अनुसार अन्तर्वार्ता, शारीरिक परीक्षा, सर्टह्यान्ड वा टाइपिङ परीक्षा हुन्छ, र अन्त्यमा कागजात जाँच हुन्छ।</p><h2>कसले आवेदन दिन सक्छ</h2><p>उमेर 1 जनवरी 2026 का आधारमा गनिन्छ; न्यूनतम उमेर 18 वा 21 वर्ष छ। धेरैजसो पदका लागि अधिकतम उमेर अनारक्षित पुरुषका लागि 40 वर्ष र योग्य महिला, SC, ST र OBC का लागि 45 वर्ष छ। फायर पदहरूमा सीमा कम छ। फायर अधिकृत र सब फायर अधिकृतका लागि अधिकतम 30 वर्ष (योग्य श्रेणीका लागि 35) र फायर अटेन्डेन्टका लागि 25 वर्ष (योग्य श्रेणीका लागि 30) छ। उम्मेदवारले आफ्नो पद र श्रेणीको सीमा सूचनामा हेर्नुपर्छ।</p><p>स्थायी बासिन्दा नियम सबैभन्दा महत्त्वपूर्ण छ। क्लास-III र क्लास-IV का पदहरू छत्तीसगढका स्थायी बासिन्दा उम्मेदवारका लागि मात्र खुला छन्। योग्य क्लास-II पदहरूमा छत्तीसगढ बाहिरका उम्मेदवारले आवेदन दिन सक्छन्, तर तिनको माथिल्लो उमेर सीमा 30 वर्ष हुन्छ। प्रमाणपत्र नभएकाले क्लास-III वा क्लास-IV पदका लागि आवेदन दिनु हुँदैन।</p><p>योग्यता पद अनुसार छ: असिस्टेन्ट इन्जिनियरका लागि चार वर्षे इन्जिनियरिङ डिग्री वा AMIE चाहिन्छ। जुनियर इन्जिनियरका लागि तीन वर्षे इन्जिनियरिङ डिप्लोमा चाहिन्छ। प्रोग्रामरका लागि कम्प्युटर विज्ञान वा सूचना प्रविधिमा इन्जिनियरिङ वा MCA चाहिन्छ। लेखा अधिकृतका लागि चार्टर्ड एकाउन्टेन्ट वा कस्ट एकाउन्टेन्ट हुनुपर्छ। चिकित्सा अधिकृतका लागि दर्तासहित MBBS डिग्री चाहिन्छ। डाटा इन्ट्री अपरेटरका लागि कम्प्युटर विज्ञान वा सूचना प्रविधि सम्बन्धी योग्यता, वा मान्यता प्राप्त कम्प्युटर योग्यतासहित स्नातक चाहिन्छ। अटेन्डेन्ट (प्लान्ट) का लागि कक्षा 10 मा दोस्रो श्रेणीसहित दुई वर्षे ITI चाहिन्छ। केही पदमा अनुभव, दर्ता वा टाइपिङ पनि मागिएको छ। योग्यता 26 नोभेम्बर 2026 सम्ममा हुनुपर्छ।</p><p>तीनवटै कम्पनीका नियमित कर्मचारीलाई शुल्क छुट छ; अरूले अनलाइन तिर्नुपर्छ, फिर्ता हुँदैन। उच्च शुल्क समूह (असिस्टेन्ट इन्जिनियर, जुनियर इन्जिनियर, अधिकृत, प्रोग्रामर र यस्तै पद) मा शुल्क अनारक्षितका लागि रु 800, OBC का लागि रु 700 र SC र ST का लागि रु 600 छ। तल्लो शुल्क समूह (डाटा इन्ट्री अपरेटर, स्टेनोग्राफर, चिकित्सा सहयोग पद, अटेन्डेन्ट र यस्तै पद) मा शुल्क अनारक्षितका लागि रु 400, OBC का लागि रु 300 र SC र ST का लागि रु 200 छ। गलत समूहको भुक्तानी फिर्ता हुँदैन।</p><h2>कसरी आवेदन दिने</h2><p>आवेदन cspc.co.in को Recruitment खण्डबाट अनलाइन मात्र दिइन्छ। पद अनुसार विज्ञापन 1/2026 वा 2/2026 को लिङ्क खोजेर इमेल र मोबाइल नम्बरका साथ दर्ता गर्नुहोस्। व्यक्तिगत, शैक्षिक तथा स्थायी बासिन्दा विवरण होसियारीपूर्वक भर्नुपर्छ, किनभने बुझाइसकेपछि सच्याउने सुविधा हुने वाचा गरिएको छैन। फोटो, हस्ताक्षर र प्रमाणपत्रका स्क्यान प्रतिहरू तयार राख्नुपर्छ।</p><p>फाराम भरेपछि 26 नोभेम्बर 2026 राति 11:55 बजेअघि शुल्क अनलाइन तिर्नुहोस्। रसिद र आवेदन सुरक्षित राख्नुहोस्, र सन्दर्भ नम्बर टिप्नुहोस् — एडमिट कार्डका लागि चाहिन्छ। छापिएको प्रति हुलाकबाट पठाउनु पर्दैन।</p><p>Growentix मा रहेका अन्य खुला सरकारी जागिरहरू पनि हेर्न सकिन्छ, जस्तै <a href='https://growentix.cloud/articles/rrc-northern-railway-act-apprentice-4651-posts-20261112'>RRC Northern Railway Apprentice Recruitment 2026</a> र <a href='https://growentix.cloud/articles/mpsc-group-c-services-16717-posts-20261111'>MPSC Group C Services Recruitment 2026</a>, दुवै नोभेम्बर 2026 मा आवेदनका लागि खुला छन्।</p><h2>सूचनामा के भनिएको छैन</h2><p>परीक्षाको मिति सूचनामा घोषणा गरिएको छैन; मिति पछि घोषणा गरिनेछ, त्यसैले अन्य वेबसाइटबाट मिति नलिनुहोस् — cspc.co.in हेर्नुहोस्। श्रेणीअनुसारको पद विभाजन सूचनाको तालिकामा छ, तर स्रोतहरूमा पूरा छापिएको थिएन — आधिकारिक PDF मा आफ्नो पद र श्रेणी हेर्नुहोस्। सूचनाका तालिका नै अन्तिम हुन्।</p><p>यस भर्तीका लागि आवेदन दिन कसैलाई पनि पैसा नतिर्नुहोस्। एक मात्र वास्तविक शुल्क cspc.co.in मा तिरिने अनलाइन आवेदन शुल्क हो, र कुनै एजेन्ट, कोचिङ सेन्टर वा सामाजिक सञ्जाल खाताले पद, मेरिट सूचीमा स्थान वा एडमिट कार्ड मिलाइदिन सक्दैन। छनोट, कागजात जाँच वा नियुक्तिका लागि पैसा माग्ने व्यक्तिलाई रिपोर्ट गर्नुहोस्, र तिनलाई कुनै कागजात, पासवर्ड वा भुक्तानी नदिनुहोस्।</p><p>स्रोतहरू: https://www.freejobalert.com/articles/csptcl-recruitment-2026-apply-online-for-1501-ae-je-deo-attendant-and-more-posts-3079324, https://www.certifica.in/jobs/cg-power-ae-je-deo-attendant-recruitment-2026, https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/education/news/cg-state-power-company-recruitment-2026-apply-online-for-1501-ae-je-and-other-posts/articleshow/135629594.cms, https://www.9curry.com/notices/718d3f</p>$$,
ARRAY['https://www.freejobalert.com/articles/csptcl-recruitment-2026-apply-online-for-1501-ae-je-deo-attendant-and-more-posts-3079324', 'https://www.certifica.in/jobs/cg-power-ae-je-deo-attendant-recruitment-2026', 'https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/education/news/cg-state-power-company-recruitment-2026-apply-online-for-1501-ae-je-and-other-posts/articleshow/135629594.cms', 'https://www.9curry.com/notices/718d3f'], NOW(), NOW(), NOW()) ON CONFLICT ("slug") DO NOTHING;

-- isro-sdsc-shar-apprentice-400-posts-20261113 (English 1646 words; Nepali 831 words)
INSERT INTO "Article" ("id", "slug", "category", "country", "titleEn", "titleNe", "excerptEn", "excerptNe", "bodyEn", "bodyNe", "sources", "publishedAt", "createdAt", "updatedAt")
VALUES
(gen_random_uuid(), 'isro-sdsc-shar-apprentice-400-posts-20261113', 'asia', 'India',
'ISRO SDSC SHAR Apprentice Recruitment 2026: 400 Posts, Apply by 26 November',
'ISRO SDSC SHAR Apprentice भर्ती 2026: 400 पद, 26 नोभेम्बर 2026 सम्म आवेदन',
'ISRO SDSC SHAR has opened 400 apprentice posts at Sriharikota for 2026. Apply online by 26 November 2026 through NATS or NAPS and UMANG. No exam, merit only.',
'ISRO SDSC SHAR मा 400 Apprentice पदका लागि आवेदन खुल्यो। 26 नोभेम्बर 2026 सम्म NATS वा NAPS र UMANG बाट आवेदन दिनुहोस्। परीक्षा छैन, मेरिट मात्र।',
$$<p>ISRO SDSC SHAR Apprentice Recruitment 2026 is now open, and the Satish Dhawan Space Centre SHAR at Sriharikota is offering 400 apprentice places to graduates, diploma holders, ITI certificate holders and vocational certificate holders from across India. The notification, numbered SDSC SHAR/SCF/P&amp;GA-II/Apprentice/2026 and dated 6 November 2026, invites online applications between 6 November and 26 November 2026. There is no written examination and no interview in this recruitment. Selection will be made through a category wise merit list based on academic marks, followed by document verification. For candidates who have been waiting for a chance to train inside the Indian Space Research Organisation, this is a direct opening, but the window is short, and the application itself has two steps that must be completed in the right order.</p>
<p>The Satish Dhawan Space Centre SHAR is the main launch centre of ISRO, so an apprenticeship there means training inside a working space establishment rather than a classroom alone. The training lasts for 12 months under the Apprentices Act, 1961, and it carries a monthly stipend that depends on the category of apprenticeship. Candidates should read the opening for what it is. This is training, not a permanent government job, and the notification makes it clear that training gives no claim to a regular, temporary or permanent post at SDSC SHAR, ISRO or the Department of Space afterwards.</p>
<h2>At a glance</h2>
<table><tr><th>Organisation</th><td>Satish Dhawan Space Centre SHAR, Sriharikota, Indian Space Research Organisation</td></tr><tr><th>Notification</th><td>SDSC SHAR/SCF/P&amp;GA-II/Apprentice/2026, dated 6 November 2026</td></tr><tr><th>Total posts</th><td>400</td></tr><tr><th>Apply dates</th><td>6 November to 26 November 2026</td></tr><tr><th>How to apply</th><td>NATS or NAPS first, then UMANG</td></tr><tr><th>Fee</th><td>Not stated in the notification</td></tr><tr><th>Age limit</th><td>No numerical age limit given</td></tr><tr><th>Selection</th><td>Merit list, then document verification, no exam, no interview</td></tr><tr><th>Stipend</th><td>Rs 9,600 to Rs 12,300 a month, by category</td></tr><tr><th>Training</th><td>12 months, Apprentices Act, 1961</td></tr></table>
<h2>What it offers</h2>
<h3>ISRO SDSC SHAR Apprentice Recruitment 2026: posts and stipend</h3>
<p>The 400 places are spread across six categories, and the largest single group is the Trade Apprentice category, with 180 places. The table below gives the full split, together with the monthly stipend for each category. One figure is deliberately left blank, because the notification does not state it, and this article does not guess it.</p>
<table><tr><th>Category</th><th>Posts</th><th>Monthly stipend</th></tr><tr><td>Engineering Graduate Apprentice</td><td>50</td><td>Rs 12,300</td></tr><tr><td>Non-Engineering Graduate Apprentice</td><td>60</td><td>Rs 12,300</td></tr><tr><td>Technician Apprentice (Diploma)</td><td>35</td><td>Rs 10,900</td></tr><tr><td>Diploma (DCCP)</td><td>60</td><td>Not stated</td></tr><tr><td>Trade Apprentice</td><td>180</td><td>Rs 9,600</td></tr><tr><td>Vocational Apprentice</td><td>15</td><td>Rs 9,600</td></tr></table>
<p>The stipend is paid every month during the 12 months of training, and the amount is fixed by category. Engineering and non-engineering graduates receive Rs 12,300 a month, technician apprentices with a diploma receive Rs 10,900 a month, and trade and vocational apprentices receive Rs 9,600 a month. The notification does not state a stipend for the Diploma (DCCP) category, so no figure is given for it here. Candidates should also note that no travel allowance is paid for document verification, and a medical fitness certificate is required at the time of joining.</p>
<p>The value of the opening is the training itself. Twelve months inside a space centre gives a trainee practical work, a stipend, and the name of a national institution on a training record. It does not give a job afterwards. The notification is plain on this point, and any person or website that promises a permanent post at ISRO after this apprenticeship is not describing this recruitment.</p>
<p>Candidates who are still in their final year, or who are waiting for a result, should also be careful. The notification ties eligibility to qualifications already held, and to a pass year of 2022 or later for graduate and diploma candidates, so a result awaited candidate cannot rely on marks that have not yet been awarded.</p>
<h2>Who can apply</h2>
<p>Only Indian nationals can apply. The eligibility rules are different for each category, and they turn on the qualification held, the marks scored, and the year of passing, so candidates should check their own category before they apply.</p>
<p>For the graduate categories, the bar is a first class pass. An Engineering Graduate Apprentice must hold a B.E. or B.Tech degree in a relevant discipline, with first class marks of at least 60 per cent or a CGPA of 6.32. A Non-Engineering Graduate Apprentice must hold a B.Sc in Maths, Physics, Chemistry, Electronics or Computer Science, or a B.Com or B.A. degree, with the same first class bar. In both cases, the candidate must have passed in 2022 or later. A Technician Apprentice must hold a diploma in a relevant discipline, again with first class marks of at least 60 per cent or a CGPA of 6.32, and must also have passed in 2022 or later.</p>
<p>Trade Apprentice places are for candidates who have passed SSLC or SSC and hold an ITI or NTC certificate from NCVT in the relevant trade. Vocational Apprentice places are for candidates who hold a two year vocational certificate recognised by AICTE. Diploma (DCCP) places are for diploma holders, and the notification gives their category separately in its table, but it does not state a stipend for them.</p>
<p>Some candidates cannot apply at all. Anyone who has completed an apprenticeship under the Apprentices Act, or is already undergoing one, is not eligible. Anyone with one year or more of work experience in any organisation is not eligible, and neither is anyone who was terminated or withdrawn from an apprenticeship, or anyone who is still pursuing higher studies. These exclusions are stated in the notification, so a candidate who falls under any of them should not apply.</p>
<h2>How to apply</h2>
<p>There are two steps, and the order matters. First, a candidate must register on the national apprenticeship portal for their category. Graduate and diploma candidates register on NATS, at nats.education.gov.in, and trade and vocational candidates register on NAPS, at apprenticeship.gov.in. Only after that registration should the candidate apply on UMANG, at web.umang.gov.in, by searching for SDSC SHAR Apprenticeship. An application made only on NATS or NAPS, without the UMANG step, is not complete.</p>
<p>Applications must be submitted between 6 November and 26 November 2026. The official website for the centre is shar.gov.in, and questions about the apprenticeship can be sent to apprenticeship@shar.gov.in. Candidates should keep their certificates, mark sheets and identity proof ready before they start, because the merit list is drawn from academic marks, and every mark claimed will be checked at document verification. No travel allowance is paid for document verification.</p>
<h2>What the notification does not say</h2>
<p>Several things that candidates usually look for are simply not in the notification, and this article does not fill the gaps. No application fee is prescribed anywhere in the notification, so no fee figure is given here. No numerical age limit is given either, so no minimum or maximum age is stated here, and the age figures that appear on some job portals are not from the notification. The stipend for the Diploma (DCCP) category is not stated. The dates of the merit list and of document verification have not been announced. Candidates should rely only on the official notification and the official portals named above, and should treat any other figure as unverified until the centre itself publishes it.</p>
<h2>A warning before you apply</h2>
<p><strong>Never pay anyone to apply.</strong> No fee is prescribed for this apprenticeship, and no agent, middleman or social media account can arrange a place on the merit list. Anyone who asks for money in exchange for an application, a merit list place, or a document verification slot is running a fraud. Apply only through NATS or NAPS and UMANG, and report any demand for payment to the authorities.</p>
